  "body": "Signup, recovery and guest artist-follow journeys retain Spanish/English selection and safe intended destinations. Recovery emails carry a validated optional redirect without changing the existing `{email}` body. Spanish policies use the existing policy version with English originals accessible. Public Live Session access validates the actual session endpoint, rejects stale replies and provides timeout/retry without losing input.\n\nThe integrated audit repairs keyboard follow actions, narrow-screen overflow, accessible field/link names and light/dark contrast, including a reproduced WebKit theme-transition failure. #406 is now merged as db69e053; its reviewed artist-only claim contract and session/navigation fences are retained. The concurrent bot change775934f75 is reconciled through a normal merge, preserving its attribution and additional person/mixed-profile tests without permitting unrelated identities.\n\nValidation:216 web suites/2074 tests before the final color-only change;43 affected tests; typecheck/build/lint and quality:repo. Final production bundle:84 cases across42 static public routes at320/1280px, zero axe/overflow/pageerror/5xx. Actual isolated PostgreSQL17 onboarding in Chromium/Firefox/WebKit verifies signup\u2192follow\u2192authoritative completion\u2192reload, keyboard Space, light/dark themes,320/390/834/1280px and200% text; Chromium verifies guest intent\u2192signup\u2192explicit confirmation with exactly one follow. Final claim union fixture passes real HTTP/PostgreSQL17. Hspec recovery5 examples/100 generated cases and pinned TLC/Alloy models/negative controls are documented. Initial bundle364315 gzip bytes/5 preloads remains under budget. These are isolated/synthetic tests, not SMTP/OAuth, field performance or full WCAG certification.\n\nRelease: backend db69e053 successfully deployed through snapshot/preflight/lease/canary/rolling; both machines healthy. This PR still needs its own exact-head gates and independent approval, then compatible backend/web release. Mobile published source efa2555 (#91) is pinned and produced Android1.0.1(9)/iOS1.0.1(18). iOS build18 is uploaded, VALID and linked to the draft; review/publication remains pending. Android submission requires the corrected existing service-account permissions. Spanish policy URLs must be deployed before mobile rollout.\n\nThe existing findings/coverage/checkpoint records remain authoritative: all initial411 coverage entries and confirmed findings remain in scope. This increment does not close the whole-platform audit. Evidence includes before/after browser results and the completed db69 guarded release report.\n\nRecovery: additive compatible API query/endpoint; no new schema migration here. Preserve migration introduction ancestry with normal merge. Revert only to a schema-compatible artifact through the guarded release lane; retain operational/payment flags and artist ownership review. Store upload, review and publication are tracked separately.\n",
